   552	  - topology or fanout contracts hidden in metadata;
   553	  - manifest-builder source that bypasses native Python control flow;
   554	  - handler-local or transitive `current_state` / `next_step` mutation;
   555	  - handler return-value routing through `route_signal`;
   556	  - runtime route dispatch from `components.py` bindings;
   557	  - manifest backend `_branch_edge_id` or equivalent handler-output routing;
   558	  - auto/CLI execution through `__megaplan_auto_phase__` or `COMMAND_HANDLERS`
   559	    as proof of native semantics;
   560	  - compatibility shell or projected-native evidence used as semantic proof;
   561	  - installed-package divergence from the checked canonical source.
   562	- Update the YAML validator so it can only pass after the semantic checker
   563	  produces row-level evidence.
   564	- Add content/provenance checks so a row cannot pass because a file exists with
   565	  the right suffix. Implemented rows need source-locatable checker evidence and
   566	  evidence hashes tied to the checked commit or installed artifact.
   567	- Make the final conformance report generated from checked evidence, not
   568	  manually asserted status.
   569	
   570	Exit gate:
   571	
   572	- The current implementation and all Phase 0 false-pass fixtures still fail the
   573	  final checker.
   574	- The corrected implementation passes by source-level evidence.
   575	- Every `implemented` row has a machine-readable evidence record containing the
   576	  row id, carrier type, source file, source span or policy object, proof test,
   577	  and content hash.
   578	- The validator rejects an otherwise well-formed ledger if the semantic checker
   579	  evidence is absent, stale, hand-authored, or points only at path existence.
   580	
   581	### Phase 9: Behavior Parity and Rollout
   582	
   583	Goal: preserve existing Megaplan behavior while changing the semantic carrier.
   584	
   585	Tasks:
   586	
   587	- Run existing golden scenarios and installed-package checks.
   588	- Add fixed deterministic scenarios for:
   589	  - prep clarification suspend/resume;
   590	  - critique/gate/revise loop and cap;
   591	  - tiebreaker proceed/iterate/escalate;
   592	  - execute DAG partial failure and resume;
   593	  - approval/no-review/deferred-human gates;
   594	  - review pass/rework/blocked/force-proceed;
   595	  - override abort/force-proceed/replan/resume/recover;
   596	  - timeout/retry/model-routing policy.
   597	- Ensure the scenario set proves split outcomes, not only happy paths:
   598	  - critical vs cosmetic cap exhaustion;
   599	  - destructive execution denied vs approved;
   600	  - blocking review cap vs advisory-only force proceed;
   601	  - recover-blocked resume with stable batch paths;
   602	  - bare/light robustness critique skip and no-review terminal routing.
   603	- Compare old and new behavior where old behavior is intended to remain.
   604	- Explicitly document intentional behavior changes.
   605	- Update final docs only after semantic and behavior gates pass.
   606	
   607	Exit gate:
   608	
   609	- Canonical source parity, behavior parity, installed-package parity, and final
   610	  documentation all agree.
   611	- The suite includes enough split-outcome scenarios to prove routing semantics,
   612	  not only artifact production.
   613	
   614	## Row Evidence Contract
   615	
   616	Every traceability row must be checked against a concrete evidence contract.
   617	The contract lives in machine-readable form next to the traceability ledger and
   618	is summarized in the final report. At minimum, every row defines:
   619	
   620	- required carrier: canonical source, declared policy, audited pure phase body,
   621	  or explicit deferral;
   622	- required source shape: branch, loop, typed outcome, subworkflow, dynamic map,
   623	  suspension gate, retry policy, timeout policy, model route, or pure phase
   624	  call;
   625	- unacceptable evidence: component constant, handler ref, route binding,
   626	  topology metadata, manifest projection, trace-only proof, or prose-only
   627	  claim;
   628	- positive test proving the final source shape;
   629	- negative fixture proving the old false pass fails;
   630	- behavior scenario proving the row still behaves correctly.
   631	- runtime path checked or compatibility path quarantined, so installed-package,
   632	  auto-drive, manifest backend, route dispatch, and CLI paths cannot silently
   633	  execute old semantics while source conformance passes.
   634	
   635	The front-half rows require explicit source evidence for prep clarification,
   636	plan artifact boundaries, critique skip/retry/fanout, gate preflight/reprompt,
   637	gate debt/fallback, and the bounded critique/gate/revise loop. The tiebreaker
   638	row requires source-visible researcher, challenger, synthesis, and decision
   639	phases. Execute and review rows require source-visible batching, approval,
   640	review fanout/fanin, retry caps, and the execute/review/rework cycle. Policy
   641	rows such as timeout, model routing, autodrive liveness, golden regeneration,
   642	and source-path reconciliation require declared, generated, or replayable
   643	evidence rather than handler or report prose.
   644	
   645	No row inherits its previous `enabled` or `implemented` status. Every row is
   646	re-proved under this contract.
   647	
   648	## Required Final Gates
   649	
   650	The corrective epic is not done until all gates pass:
   651	
   652	1. `workflow.pypeline` has no component constants as product-control skeleton.
   653	2. No report-owned semantic is solely carriered by `components.py`.
   654	3. No report-owned semantic is solely carriered by handler refs, route labels,
   655	   manifests, native traces, or runtime side effects.
   656	4. Every traceability row has machine-checked source/policy/pure-body evidence.
   657	5. The current pre-correction implementation fails as a negative fixture.
   658	6. The generated conformance report cannot claim `implemented` for a row unless
   659	   the semantic checker emitted proof for that row.
   660	7. Installed-package source-path reconciliation proves the shipped artifact uses
   661	   the same canonical `.pypeline`.
   662	8. Behavior parity tests pass or intentional differences are named with the old
   663	   behavior, new behavior, reason, affected scenarios, and reviewer signoff.
   664	9. Human-readable topology/rendered views derive from canonical source.
   665	10. A reviewer can inspect canonical source and understand the complete
   666	    Megaplan product flow without reading handler-local state transitions.
   667	11. `workflow.py`, compatibility shells, `Pipeline.native_program` projections,
   668	    manifest backends, route dispatch, and CLI phase dispatch are either
   669	    proven non-semantic for the corrected workflow or explicitly quarantined
   670	    as legacy execution paths.
   671	12. Prior conformance reports cannot be used as proof artifacts except as
   672	    historical baseline/failure evidence.
   673	13. `build_pipeline()` no longer discards the lowered `.pypeline` topology for
   674	    canonical Megaplan, or it is quarantined as a legacy builder with a new
   675	    canonical builder in place.
   676	14. Any deliberate narrowing of the end-state target includes both a checker
   677	    rule that still blocks the original false-pass pattern and a behavior
   678	    scenario proving the narrowed carrier cannot smuggle routing.
   679	
   680	## Suggested Epic Breakdown
   681	
   682	The active cloud initiative compresses the work into seven busy two-week
   683	sprints. This is a schedule compression, not a scope reduction: the original
   684	phase plan above remains authoritative for detailed content, and the active
   685	briefs under
   686	`.megaplan/initiatives/megaplan-native-parity-corrective/briefs/s*.md` name
   687	which earlier milestone scope they absorb.
   688	
   689	### Sprint 1: Checker, Outcomes, Builder Slice
   690	
   691	Build the checker, negative fixtures, typed outcome/interface boundary, and one
   692	runtime-load-bearing `.pypeline` vertical slice. This combines the old semantic
   693	checker, typed domain model, and canonical builder slice work because the
   694	checker cannot be trusted until it proves a real source-derived runtime edge.
   695	
   696	Deliverables:
   697	
   698	- semantic checker skeleton and current-pattern negative fixture;
   699	- row-to-evidence schema and baseline gap report;
   700	- typed outcomes and retained-handler interfaces;
   701	- `build_pipeline()` or replacement builder consuming lowered `.pypeline`
   702	  topology for at least one real edge;
   703	- dead-delete mutation and installed-package proof for that edge.
   704	
   705	### Sprint 2: Front-Half Native Loop
   706	
   707	Extract prep, plan, critique, gate, revise, and the coupled front-half loop.
   708	
   709	Deliverables:
   710	
   711	- native front-half source;
   712	- prep clarify, gate downgrade, cap exhaustion, and force-proceed scenarios;
   713	- component/handler carrier deletion or quarantine for implemented front-half
   714	  rows;
   715	- row-level checker evidence for the front half.
   716	
   717	### Sprint 3: Tiebreaker And Replan Native Flow
   718	
   719	Extract tiebreaker into a real native subworkflow and make replan rejoin normal
   720	planning/finalize behavior.
   721	
   722	Deliverables:
   723	
   724	- researcher/challenger/synthesis/decision source structure;
   725	- tiebreaker proceed/iterate/escalate/replan scenarios;
   726	- path checkpoint tests;
   727	- dead-delete proof for old tiebreaker carriers.
   728	
   729	### Sprint 4: Execute DAG, Approval, Resume
   730	
   731	Extract dependency-aware execution, deterministic batching, approval gates,
   732	blocked recovery, no-review terminal routing, and partial resume.
   733	
   734	Deliverables:
   735	
   736	- execute native subworkflow or visible source/policy batching;
   737	- DAG/batch fixtures and stable checkpoint tests;
   738	- destructive approval and recover-blocked scenarios;
   739	- source-visible blocked/partial-failure/resume branches.
   740	
   741	### Sprint 5: Review, Rework, Finalize
   742	
   743	Extract review fanout/fanin, retry caps, blocked/force-proceed outcomes, human
   744	verification, explicit execute/review/rework loop, and finalize fallback
   745	routing.
   746	
   747	Deliverables:
   748	
   749	- review native subworkflow and explicit rework cycle;
   750	- blocking vs advisory cap scenarios;
   751	- human verification and finalize fallback scenarios;
   752	- review/finalize component carrier quarantine or deletion.
   753	
   754	### Sprint 6: Override, Auto, Compatibility Collapse
   755	
   756	Extract routing overrides, remove auto-drive as a second route brain, and
   757	collapse or fence remaining semantic compatibility paths.
   758	
