     1	# Megaplan Native Parity Corrective North Star
     2	
     3	Canonical Megaplan must become source-authoritative native workflow code.
     4	
     5	The final semantic authority is:
     6	
     7	- `arnold_pipelines/megaplan/workflows/workflow.pypeline`;
     8	- named native subworkflows imported by that source;
     9	- declared policies attached to named source constructs;
    10	- retained pure phase bodies behind typed interfaces.
    11	
    12	The final system must not require `components.py`, route bindings, handler refs,
    13	manifest backend route translation, `Pipeline.native_program` compatibility
    14	projections, auto-drive next-step derivation, or CLI command handlers to
    15	understand report-owned product topology.
    16	
    17	The intended end state is described by
    18	`docs/arnold/megaplan-native-representation-report.md`; the current-state map is
    19	`docs/arnold/megaplan-native-current-codebase-map.md`; the execution plan is
    20	`docs/arnold/megaplan-native-parity-corrective-plan.md`; the substrate
    21	decision/judgement layer is `docs/arnold/megaplan-native-oracle-synthesis.md`.
    22	
    23	## Non-Negotiables
    24	
    25	- The current component-call skeleton fails the semantic checker before any
    26	  extraction milestone can close.
    27	- Canonical Megaplan executes through `.pypeline` lowering into the existing
    28	  DSL/manifest runtime for this corrective epic.
    29	- `build_pipeline()` must consume lowered `.pypeline` topology or be replaced /
    30	  quarantined before broad extraction can close.
    31	- Each traceability row is re-proved from row-level source/policy/pure-body
    32	  evidence. No row inherits old `enabled` or `implemented` status.
    33	- Components, handlers, manifests, graph projections, traces, auto-drive, and
    34	  CLI are consumers/adapters. They are not semantic authority.
    35	- Each milestone deletes or quarantines the component/handler carriers it
    36	  replaces. Component collapse is incremental, not a final big-bang cleanup.
    37	- Behavior parity is proven with split-outcome scenarios, not happy-path smoke
    38	  tests.
    39	- Any narrowing of the end-state target must include both a checker rule that
    40	  still blocks the old false-pass pattern and a behavior scenario proving the
    41	  narrowed carrier cannot smuggle routing.
    42	
    43	## Done Means
    44	
    45	The canonical `.pypeline` source and named subworkflows visibly own prep,
    46	critique, gate, revise, tiebreaker, finalize, execute, review, override, human
    47	gates, retries, model routing, suspension, and resume. A reviewer can follow the
    48	workflow without reading handler-local state transitions or component route
    49	tables, and installed-package execution follows the same source-derived
    50	semantics.
