     1	# M1 - Semantic Checker Baseline
     2	
     3	## Objective
     4	
     5	Build the first production semantic checker and make the current
     6	`workflow.pypeline` fail for the right reasons. This milestone prevents the
     7	epic from starting with another native-looking wrapper.
     8	
     9	## Anchors
    10	
    11	- `docs/arnold/megaplan-native-representation-report.md`
    12	- `docs/arnold/megaplan-native-current-codebase-map.md`
    13	- `docs/arnold/megaplan-native-oracle-synthesis.md`
    14	- `docs/arnold/megaplan-native-parity-corrective-plan.md`
    15	
    16	## Files To Change And Instructions
    17	
    18	- Add a semantic checker under an appropriate Arnold/Megaplan testable module.
    19	  It must run against canonical `.pypeline` source and installed-package source.
    20	- Add checker diagnostics for:
    21	  - component-call skeletons;
    22	  - `handler_ref` / `route_bindings`;
    23	  - policy-as-route-table;
    24	  - projected-native proof;
    25	  - handler `current_state` / `next_step` / `route_signal` ownership;
    26	  - runtime route dispatch via `route_dispatch` or manifest backend edge maps.
    27	- Add row-evidence schema scaffolding for traceability rows.
    28	- Add a baseline gap report documenting which current rows are source-owned,
    29	  policy-owned, or still component/handler/runtime-owned.
    30	- Add a compatibility-path inventory covering `workflow.py`, `build_pipeline()`,
    31	  compatibility shells, manifest backend, route dispatch, auto, CLI handlers,
    32	  direct handlers, and installed package paths.
    33	
    34	## Verifiable Completion Criterion
    35	
    36	- The current `workflow.pypeline` fails the semantic checker.
    37	- At least one negative fixture represents the current component-call skeleton.
    38	- The checker emits machine-readable evidence or failure records by row.
    39	- The checker runs against checkout source and an installed package artifact.
    40	- No later milestone can mark a row `implemented` without row-evidence schema.
    41	
    42	## Native Parity Alignment
    43	
    44	- This milestone should not extract product semantics yet.
    45	- It is valid only if it prevents a future false closeout based on path
    46	  existence, source shape, or generated reports.
    47	
===== .megaplan/initiatives/megaplan-native-parity-corrective/briefs/m10-final-conformance-rollout.md
     1	# M10 - Final Conformance Rollout
     2	
     3	## Objective
     4	
     5	Generate final semantic conformance evidence from checked source, behavior
     6	scenarios, installed-package execution, and quarantined compatibility paths.
     7	
     8	## Files To Change And Instructions
     9	
    10	- Semantic checker and conformance validator
    11	  Make final ledger/report generation consume checker evidence. Reject stale,
    12	  hand-authored, path-only, or report-only implemented rows.
    13	- Traceability artifacts
    14	  Re-prove every row. No old `enabled` or `implemented` status is inherited.
    15	- Docs
    16	  Update end-state/current-state/corrective docs where implementation made
    17	  deliberate narrowing decisions. Any narrowing requires a checker rule and
    18	  behavior scenario.
    19	- Tests
    20	  Run full deterministic scenario suite, installed-package source check,
    21	  topology regeneration, handler-purity scan, compatibility quarantine checks,
    22	  and dead-delete mutation checks.
    23	
    24	## Verifiable Completion Criterion
    25	
    26	- Generated conformance report cannot mark a row implemented without checker
    27	  evidence.
    28	- Installed package uses the same canonical `.pypeline` source and semantics.
    29	- All split-outcome behavior scenarios pass.
    30	- Prior conformance reports are preserved only as historical baseline/failure
    31	  evidence.
    32	- The final state satisfies the North Star and
    33	  `docs/arnold/megaplan-native-representation-report.md` or records deliberate
    34	  narrowing with checker and behavior proof.
    35	
===== .megaplan/initiatives/megaplan-native-parity-corrective/briefs/m2-typed-outcomes-and-interfaces.md
     1	# M2 - Typed Outcomes And Interfaces
     2	
     3	## Objective
     4	
     5	Define the typed domain boundary that lets native source route on explicit
     6	outcomes instead of raw handler strings.
     7	
     8	## Files To Change And Instructions
     9	
    10	- Add closed outcome types for gate, tiebreaker, review, override, suspension,
    11	  halt, execute, and finalize outcomes.
    12	- Keep raw string labels only in compatibility serialization adapters.
    13	- Add retained-handler interface/protocol definitions based on
    14	  `arnold_pipelines/megaplan/native_interfaces.py` where useful.
    15	- Add transitive handler-purity scanner support: retained handlers declare
    16	  allowed side effects, and the scanner checks callees for report-owned routing.
    17	- Add tests proving unsupported outcome values fail authoring or validation.
    18	
    19	## Verifiable Completion Criterion
    20	
    21	- Canonical source can branch on typed outcomes.
    22	- Report-owned decisions do not branch on raw string literals.
    23	- Every retained handler boundary has a typed input/output contract and an
    24	  allowed-side-effect declaration.
    25	- The semantic checker can distinguish typed outcome routing from compatibility
    26	  string serialization.
    27	
    28	## Native Parity Alignment
    29	
    30	- This milestone enables extraction; it does not claim row implementation
    31	  unless the row's source structure and behavior scenario already pass.
    32	
===== .megaplan/initiatives/megaplan-native-parity-corrective/briefs/m3-canonical-builder-vertical-slice.md
     1	# M3 - Canonical Builder Vertical Slice
     2	
     3	## Objective
     4	
     5	Make `.pypeline` lowering runtime-load-bearing before broad extraction.
     6	`build_pipeline()` currently risks discarding lowered topology and rebuilding
     7	runtime behavior from `components.py`; this milestone closes that false-pass
     8	path for at least one real slice.
     9	
    10	## Files To Change And Instructions
    11	
    12	- `arnold_pipelines/megaplan/workflows/planning.py`
    13	  Make `build_pipeline()` consume lowered `.pypeline` topology for a real edge
    14	  such as prep to plan, or introduce a new canonical builder for that slice.
    15	- Compatibility/projection code
    16	  Ensure compatibility shells consume the source-derived slice or are explicitly
    17	  marked legacy for that slice.
    18	- Semantic checker
    19	  Add dead-delete mutation tests disabling old component-derived routing for the
    20	  selected slice.
    21	- Installed package tests
    22	  Prove the installed package follows the same source-derived slice.
    23	
    24	## Verifiable Completion Criterion
    25	
    26	- The selected slice executes from lowered `.pypeline` topology.
    27	- Disabling old component route bindings for that slice does not change the
    28	  corrected deterministic trace.
    29	- Runtime behavior, checker evidence, and installed-package evidence agree.
    30	
    31	## Native Parity Alignment
    32	
    33	- This milestone is the guardrail against decorative source extraction. Broad
    34	  source migration should not proceed until this slice proves the builder seam.
    35	
