===== .megaplan/initiatives/megaplan-native-parity-corrective/briefs/s1-checker-outcomes-builder-slice.md
     1	# S1 - Checker, Outcomes, Builder Slice
     2	
     3	## Objective
     4	
     5	Establish the anti-false-pass foundation in one busy sprint: semantic checker,
     6	typed outcome/interface boundary, and a real source-derived runtime vertical
     7	slice. This sprint absorbs the old M1, M2, and M3 without dropping any guardrail.
     8	
     9	## Legacy 10-Sprint Source Mapping
    10	
    11	- Absorbs `m1-semantic-checker-baseline.md`.
    12	- Absorbs `m2-typed-outcomes-and-interfaces.md`.
    13	- Absorbs `m3-canonical-builder-vertical-slice.md`.
    14	
    15	The original briefs remain in this directory as source artifacts. Treat this
    16	brief as the launch contract and the original three briefs as detailed scope
    17	appendices.
    18	
    19	## Anchors
    20	
    21	- `docs/arnold/megaplan-native-representation-report.md`
    22	- `docs/arnold/megaplan-native-current-codebase-map.md`
    23	- `docs/arnold/megaplan-native-oracle-synthesis.md`
    24	- `docs/arnold/megaplan-native-parity-corrective-plan.md`
    25	
    26	## Work Required
    27	
    28	- Build the first production semantic checker against canonical `.pypeline`
    29	  source and installed-package source.
    30	- Make the current component-call skeleton fail for the right reasons:
    31	  component-call topology, `handler_ref`, `route_bindings`, policy-as-route
    32	  table, projected-native proof, handler-owned `current_state` / `next_step` /
    33	  `route_signal`, route dispatch, and manifest backend edge maps.
    34	- Add row-evidence schema scaffolding. No later sprint may mark a row
    35	  implemented without row-level source/policy/pure-body evidence.
    36	- Add closed typed outcomes and retained-handler interfaces for gate,
    37	  tiebreaker, review, override, suspension, halt, execute, and finalize.
    38	- Confine raw string labels to compatibility serialization adapters.
    39	- Add retained-handler purity/side-effect declarations and checker support.
    40	- Make `.pypeline` lowering runtime-load-bearing for at least one real edge
    41	  such as prep to plan. `build_pipeline()` must consume lowered topology for
    42	  that slice or be replaced/quarantined for that slice.
    43	- Add dead-delete mutation tests disabling old component-derived routing for
    44	  the selected slice.
    45	- Prove checkout source and installed package source behave the same for the
    46	  selected slice.
    47	- Produce baseline gap and compatibility inventory covering `workflow.py`,
    48	  `build_pipeline()`, compatibility shells, manifest backend, route dispatch,
    49	  auto, CLI handlers, direct handlers, and installed package paths.
    50	
    51	## Verifiable Completion Criterion
    52	
    53	- Current `workflow.pypeline` fails semantic checking before correction.
    54	- At least one negative fixture captures the old component-call skeleton.
    55	- The checker emits machine-readable evidence/failure records by row.
    56	- Canonical source can branch on typed outcomes, and report-owned branches do
    57	  not route on raw string literals.
    58	- The selected runtime slice executes from lowered `.pypeline` topology.
    59	- Disabling old component route bindings for that slice does not change the
    60	  corrected deterministic trace.
    61	- Runtime behavior, checker evidence, and installed-package evidence agree.
    62	
    63	## Do Not Close If
    64	
    65	- The checker only validates file existence or generated reports.
    66	- `build_pipeline()` still silently rebuilds the selected slice from
    67	  `components.py`.
    68	- Any row gets an inherited `enabled` or `implemented` status from prior
    69	  reports.
===== .megaplan/initiatives/megaplan-native-parity-corrective/briefs/s2-front-half-native-loop.md
     1	# S2 - Front-Half Native Loop
     2	
     3	## Objective
     4	
     5	Extract prep, plan, critique, gate, and revise-loop semantics into canonical
     6	source and declared policy. This sprint is intentionally coupled: gate and
     7	revise are one loop, and splitting them is how the previous false pass stayed
     8	plausible.
     9	
    10	## Legacy 10-Sprint Source Mapping
    11	
    12	- Absorbs `m4-front-half-source-extraction.md`.
    13	- Uses the typed boundary and builder slice from S1.
