    38	  thresholds, and hidden finalize fallback routing.
    39	
    40	## Do Not Close If
    41	
    42	- Review or finalize routing is still inferred from state fields written by
    43	  handlers.
    44	- No-review terminal behavior depends on handler/private robustness overrides
    45	  instead of source/policy-visible branches.
===== .megaplan/initiatives/megaplan-native-parity-corrective/briefs/s6-override-auto-compat-collapse.md
     1	# S6 - Override, Auto, Compatibility Collapse
     2	
     3	## Objective
     4	
     5	Extract routing override actions into native source, remove auto-drive as a
     6	second route brain, and collapse/quarantine remaining component, handler,
     7	manifest, and compatibility paths that formerly owned report-level semantics.
     8	
     9	## Legacy 10-Sprint Source Mapping
    10	
    11	- Absorbs `m8-override-control-surface.md`.
    12	- Absorbs `m9-component-collapse-compat-quarantine.md`.
    13	- Includes the "delete as you extract" refinement from the oracle synthesis:
    14	  any carrier replaced in earlier sprints must already be deleted or fenced;
    15	  this sprint finishes what remains and proves the global fence.
    16	
    17	## Work Required
    18	
    19	- Make routing overrides source-visible:
    20	  abort, force proceed, replan, resume/recover paths, terminal halt behavior.
    21	- Leave config/effect-only overrides as audited effects only when they cannot
    22	  route: set model/profile/vendor/robustness, add note, non-routing state
    23	  annotations.
    24	- Declare authority requirements at routing control gates.
    25	- Remove or fence `LEGACY_ALIASES` into handler-private routing functions.
    26	- Remove report-owned route bindings, topology contracts, fanout/reducer
    27	  contracts, handler refs, and override dispatch metadata from `components.py`,
    28	  or mark them compatibility-only with tests proving no influence over corrected
    29	  flow.
    30	- Delete decision translators in `manifest_backend.py`, `route_dispatch.py`,
    31	  `auto.py`, and CLI dispatch, or quarantine as explicit legacy paths.
    32	- Ensure auto-drive may emit operational events only; it must consume canonical
    33	  workflow events and must not derive product routes from state.
    34	- Prove compatibility shells and projected native programs consume canonical
    35	  source-derived semantics or cannot satisfy traceability rows.
    36	
    37	## Verifiable Completion Criterion
    38	
    39	- Scenarios pass:
    40	  - force-proceed from blocked reaches finalization/done;
    41	  - abort mid-loop reaches terminal aborted;
    42	  - recover/resume routes do not depend on handler-private dispatch.
    43	- Deleting/quarantining semantic metadata from `components.py` does not change
    44	  deterministic corrected product-routing traces.
    45	- Adapters that translate decisions are gone or legacy-fenced. Adapters that
    46	  translate data may remain.
    47	- No implemented row cites components, handler refs, route bindings, manifest
    48	  backend routing, auto next-step derivation, CLI handlers, or projected-native
    49	  shells as proof.
    50	
    51	## Do Not Close If
    52	
    53	- Auto-drive still derives the next product step from state.
    54	- A compatibility bridge can satisfy semantic evidence without going through
    55	  canonical source.
===== .megaplan/initiatives/megaplan-native-parity-corrective/briefs/s7-final-conformance-rollout.md
     1	# S7 - Final Conformance Rollout
     2	
     3	## Objective
     4	
     5	Generate final semantic conformance evidence from checked source, behavior
     6	scenarios, installed-package execution, and quarantined compatibility paths.
     7	Close the epic only if the North Star is genuinely reached or any deliberate
     8	narrowing is proved by checker rule plus behavior scenario.
     9	
    10	## Legacy 10-Sprint Source Mapping
    11	
    12	- Absorbs `m10-final-conformance-rollout.md`.
    13	- Re-validates every old M1-M10 acceptance criterion against the compressed
    14	  seven-sprint implementation.
    15	
    16	## Work Required
    17	
    18	- Make final ledger/report generation consume checker evidence. Reject stale,
    19	  hand-authored, path-only, or report-only implemented rows.
    20	- Re-prove every traceability row. No old `enabled` or `implemented` status is
    21	  inherited.
    22	- Run the full deterministic split-outcome scenario suite, including:
    23	  - prep clarify suspend/resume;
    24	  - gate reprompt/downgrade;
    25	  - critical vs cosmetic cap exhaustion;
    26	  - tiebreaker replan/rejoin;
    27	  - execute blocked batch recover/resume;
    28	  - destructive approval gate;
    29	  - review rework cycle;
    30	  - blocking vs advisory review cap;
    31	  - no-review terminal path;
    32	  - override force-proceed and abort.
    33	- Run installed-package source check, topology regeneration, handler-purity
    34	  scan, compatibility quarantine checks, and dead-delete mutation checks.
    35	- Validate resume identity and serialized-state consumer compatibility for
    36	  human gates, tiebreaker pending, execute approvals, and blocked recovery.
    37	- Pin or hash deterministic prompt/model fixtures used in behavior scenarios,
    38	  or document refresh rules that prevent stale-fixture false confidence.
    39	- Update end-state/current-state/corrective docs where implementation made
    40	  deliberate narrowing decisions.
    41	- Keep prior conformance reports only as historical baseline/failure evidence.
    42	
    43	## Verifiable Completion Criterion
    44	
    45	- Generated conformance report cannot mark a row implemented without checker
    46	  evidence.
    47	- Installed package uses the same canonical `.pypeline` source and semantics.
    48	- All split-outcome behavior scenarios pass.
    49	- Compatibility paths are either deleted, data-only adapters, or fenced legacy
    50	  paths that cannot satisfy row evidence.
    51	- Final state satisfies the North Star and
    52	  `docs/arnold/megaplan-native-representation-report.md`, or records deliberate
    53	  narrowing with checker and behavior proof.
    54	
    55	## Do Not Close If
    56	
    57	- Any report-owned route is still owned by components, handlers, manifest edge
    58	  maps, auto next-step derivation, CLI dispatch, or projected-native
    59	  compatibility.
    60	- The final report is hand-maintained next to conflicting prose documents.

