ey/Documents/megaplan, complete the native Python pipeline migration described in docs/arnold/pipelines/migration-completion-plan-v3.md.\n\nThe codebase contains:\n- arnold/pipeline/native/ — compiler, runtime, graph projection\n- arnold/pipeline/executor.py — neutral executor dispatch\n- arnold/pipelines/megaplan/pipeline.py — canonical megaplan pipeline\n- arnold/pipelines/megaplan/pipelines/{creative,doc,jokes,live_supervisor,writing_panel_strict,epic_blitz,select_tournament}\n- arnold/pipelines/folder_audit\n- arnold/pipelines/deliberation\n- arnold/pipelines/evidence_pack\n- arnold/pipelines/megaplan/_pipeline/ — legacy graph-era internals\n\nGoal: make every registered pipeline native-first, add a Pipeline.native_program field while keeping resource_bundles compatibility during transition, update registry/manifest discovery/validator/CLI, migrate evidence_pack, clean tests/golden traces/docs, then purge the old graph-era code.\n\nDo not invent external modules. Work only with files that exist in this repo.","idea_snapshot_path":"idea_snapshot.md","iteration":1,"last_gate":{"orchestrator_guidance":"First iteration; follow gate recommendation: PROCEED. Verify unresolved flags against the plan and project code before accepting.","passed":true,"preflight_results":{"claude_available":true,"codex_available":true,"project_dir_exists":true,"project_dir_writable":true,"success_criteria_present":true},"rationale":"All three significant flags are resolvable. correctness-1 is factually misaligned with the current codebase: manifest.py line 296 already enforces bare-symbol entrypoints via 'entrypoint not in top_level_symbols', and zero module:name patterns exist anywhere. correctness-3 is also unsupported by evidence: no dynamic import patterns (importlib.import_module, __import__, or getattr-based module resolution) reference any _pipeline module — every _pipeline import is a static import/from statement that rg will catch. correctness-2 is the only real concern (evidence pack ordering differences between native and legacy execution), but it is an implementation detail the worker can address by normalizing output ordering during parity test construction. The plan is sound enough to proceed; remaining risks are manageable during implementation.","recommendation":"PROCEED","reprompted":false,"settled_decisions":[{"decision":"ARNOLD_FORCE_LEGACY=true is the canonical graph fallback flag; ARNOLD_PIPELINE_RUNTIME=graph is preserved only as a deprecated compatibility alias during transition.","id":"SD1","rationale":"The plan and migration doc both specify ARNOLD_FORCE_LEGACY as the explicit fallback. Consolidating to one flag reduces confusion and simplifies executor dispatch logic in Step 2."},{"decision":"Bare-symbol entrypoints (e.g., 'build_pipeline') are the required manifest format for all native-backed packages; module:name entrypoints are rejected at manifest validation time.","id":"SD2","rationale":"The manifest validator already enforces this at line 296. No existing manifests use module:name format. The plan formalizes existing behavior rather than introducing a breaking change."},{"decision":"Native execution is the default and canonical runtime path; no environment flag (ARNOLD_NATIVE_RUNTIME) is required to enable it. Graph execution is only reachable via ARNOLD_FORCE_LEGACY=true.","id":"SD3","rationale":"This is the core architectural premise of the migration: native-first, graph-as-fallback. The plan's Phase 1 Steps 2-3 implement this by removing opt-in flag assumptions and wiring executor dispatch to prefer Pipeline.native_program."}],"signals_assessment":"Weighted score 6.0 on iteration 1, with 3 open significant flags all in the correctness category. Preflight checks passed (directory exists, writable, Criteria present). The critique worker partially degraded on scope/prerequisite_ordering checks, but those are meta-concerns about plan structure rather than blocking flaws. No recurring critiques or addressed-then-reopened flags. The plan delta is null (first iteration). Flag concerns are specific and tractable rather than systemic.","warnings":["critique degraded: high-complexity check(s) unverifiable (scope, prerequisite_ordering); operator attention required before treating critique as complete.","Evidence pack parity tests (Phase 4) must include JSON key-sorting or other ordering normalization to guarantee deterministic output comparison between native and legacy paths.","The manifest entrypoint enforcement described in Step 4 is already partially implemented; the implementation worker should verify manifest.py validation is sufficient rather than re-implementing it.","Phase 5 golden trace regeneration may surface subtle behavioral differences between native and graph execution; budget time for investigation if snapshot diffs appear beyond ordering."]},"meta":{"critique_unverifiable_checks":[{"checks":[{"attention":"high_complexity_unverifiable","complexity":4,"id":"scope","question":"Search for related code that handles the same concept. Is the reported issue a symptom of something broader — and is any single step sized to fit one worker turn?","reason":"parallel critique worker failed for check 'scope': Hermes worker failed for step 'critique': worker_structural_audit_failed: model output structural audit failed: additional_property at /name: unexpected property 'name'; additional_property at /path: unexpected property 'path'; additional_property at /tool_call_id: unexpected property 'tool_call_id'"},{"attention":"high_complexity_unverifiable","complexity":4,"id":"prerequisite_ordering","question":"Do tasks that depend on a precondition gracefully handle that precondition only partially holding?","reason":"parallel critique worker failed for check 'prerequisite_ordering': Repair retry for critique did not return valid JSON at line 1 col 1"}],"iteration":1,"warnings":["critique degraded: high-complexity check(s) unverifiable (scope, prerequisite_ordering); operator attention r