.megaplan/plans/pipeline-week1-cleanup/gate_signals_v5.json:5:    "idea": "# Pipeline Week 1 Cleanup\n\n## Outcome\n\nMake pipeline modules describe topology, not compatibility shims or inline\nworkflow mechanics.\n\n## Scope\n\nIn scope:\n\n- Remove planning compatibility shims entirely.\n- Keep `compile_planning_pipeline()` as the only planning compiler.\n- Split doc and creative pipeline step shells into dedicated modules.\n- Make the creative pipeline table-driven.\n- Remove duplicate judges artifact path plumbing.\n- Update focused tests and docs that referenced removed shim APIs.\n\nOut of scope:\n\n- Unrelated execution, review, worker, profile, and ticket changes already\n  present in the worktree.\n- Broad desloppify queue work.\n- Public backward-compat wrappers for the removed planning APIs.\n\n## Locked Decisions\n\n- No shims.\n- No compatibility wrappers.\n- No legacy overlay path.\n- First-class `doc` and `creative` pipelines are the mode path.\n- Pipeline `__init__.py` files should primarily expose metadata and\n  `build_pipeline()`.\n\n## Done Criteria\n\n- Targeted pipeline tests pass.\n- `rg` finds no in-tree imports of `compile_pipeline_for`, `mode_overlay`,\n  `robustness_overlay`, `with_prep_overlay`, `with_feedback_overlay`,\n  `_step_for`, or `_RuntimeStep`, except historical docs that are explicitly\n  updated or clearly archived.\n- Unrelated dirty files are left untouched.",
.megaplan/plans/pipeline-week1-cleanup/gate_signals_v5.json:26:        "concern": "Did the work fully address the issue hints, user notes, and approved plan requirements?: Creative run path: the plan says to preserve form validation, form-specific prompt keys like `execute_creative:joke`, and primary criterion propagation, but `megaplan/_pipeline/run_cli.py` has no `--form` or `--primary-criterion` options and calls `get_pipeline(pipeline_name)`, whose registry builder invokes `build_pipeline()` with no keyword arguments. That means `megaplan run creative --form poem` cannot work through the first-class pipeline path without additional CLI and registry-builder plumbing, despite tests and docs describing that surface.",
.megaplan/plans/pipeline-week1-cleanup/gate_signals_v5.json:46:        "concern": "Does the change touch all locations AND supporting infrastructure?: Existing creative pipeline tests are a concrete location the plan needs to update: `tests/pipelines/test_creative_pipeline.py` currently asserts that `build_pipeline(form='poem')` produces `prep:poem`, `execute_creative:poem`, `critique_creative:poem`, and `revise_creative:poem`. The revised plan says non-joke forms should use generic prompt keys, but it does not name this stale test as an update target, so an implementer following only the listed test additions could leave contradictory assertions in place until validation fails.",
.megaplan/plans/pipeline-week1-cleanup/gate_signals_v5.json:51:        "concern": "Find the callers of the changed function. What arguments do they actually pass? Does the fix handle all of them?: The registry caller contract is nullary: `PipelineBuilder = Callable[[], Pipeline]`, `PipelineRegistry.get()` calls `self.builders[name]()`, and discovered pipeline builders are stored directly. This handles `build_pipeline()` defaults but cannot pass `form='poem'` or `primary_criterion='...'` to `megaplan.pipelines.creative.build_pipeline`, so only the default joke form is reachable through `get_pipeline('creative')` today.",
.megaplan/plans/pipeline-week1-cleanup/gate_signals_v5.json:67:        "resolution": "`_run_pipeline()` calls `preflight_or_raise()` before `_build_pipeline_for_run(args)`. A direct `cli_run` with invalid creative form returned credential preflight code 7 in this environment; with preflight patched, `CliError invalid_args` propagated from `_build_pipeline_for_run()`."
.megaplan/plans/pipeline-week1-cleanup/gate_signals_v5.json:71:        "concern": "Creative option scope: set creative-only options are silently accepted for non-creative pipelines because the parser adds them globally and `_build_pipeline_for_run()` ignores them unless `pipeline_name == 'creative'`.",
