     1	"""Source compiler foundation for Python-shaped workflow authoring.
     2	
     3	This module owns source-oriented parsing data, resolver boundaries, spans, and
     4	result carriers.  It is intentionally separate from ``arnold.workflow.compiler``:
     5	that module lowers explicit DSL objects to manifests, while this one parses
     6	Python-shaped source into compiler-owned intermediate data.
     7	
     8	Author-facing workflow source files use either the ``.py`` or ``.pypeline``
     9	suffix.  Both suffixes carry Python-shaped AST source and are parsed
    10	identically; source spans, diagnostics, and manifest identity are preserved
    11	regardless of suffix.  The ``.pypeline`` suffix is the author-facing convention
    12	for explicit-node product workflows.
    13	
    14	Ownership:
